OrionLayer open fix 99 — a bitmap line too short for its picture
=================================================================

Work order 295 (Data, 17 October 2026: "repariere zuerst die Engine").
orion2re on the fork's branch `orionlayer` (v2.0.0), on top of open fix
98; commit 29047f2d. Not on `orionlayer-local`. Not under ORION2RE_EXT:
it is a crash, with or without a client.

bitmap::Draw_Bitmap_Line (bitmap.cpp, the 1.60 source :298-470) draws a
picture stretched along a line: scale_factor = line_len * 100 / width
(:336), later (rx - mid_x) * 100 / scale_factor (:458). A line shorter
than a hundredth of the picture's width makes scale_factor 0 and the
second an integer division by zero — SIGFPE in the game thread, the engine
gone without a message. CMBTSPEC::Draw_Clipped_Tractor_Line clips a
tractor beam to the screen first (cmbtspec.cpp:56): seen live in work
order 295 (g293_diablo_fight, a 4K battle; core of 17 October 2026 20:17,
PID 109391), the beam cut to (0,350)-(0,349), line_len 1, the tractor
picture 129 px wide. The same code stands in the 1.60 source.

The line returns before the render buffer is locked when width <= 0 or
line_len * 100 / width == 0: nothing of such a line would be drawn (its
picture scaled to 0 %). Every other line draws as before.

